From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+openwrt@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: wed: log the WDMA init handshake at debug

WED_EXT_INT_STATUS_RX_DRV_INIT_WDMA_EN (bit 19) is part of the error
mask shared with the vendor driver and with mainline, but this WED
enables the WDMA RX DMA, and the RX driver raises the bit once when it
comes up.  Every start therefore logs "error status=00080000" for what
is the handshake of a working initialisation.

Keep the mask as it is - an unexpected bit 19 still has to be acked and
must not be lost if it ever means something else - and only change how
it is reported: a lone bit 19 goes to debug, anything else stays on the
error line, with bit 19 included when it arrives together with a real
fault.

Signed-off-by: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+openwrt@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_wed.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_wed.c
@@ -1097,8 +1097,21 @@ static u32 airoha_wed_irq_get(struct mtk
 	val = wed_r32(dev, WED_EXT_INT_STATUS);
 	wed_w32(dev, WED_EXT_INT_STATUS, val);
 	val &= WED_EXT_INT_STATUS_ERROR_MASK;
-	if (val && net_ratelimit())
-		pr_err("airoha_wed%d: error status=%08x\n", dev->hw->index, val);
+	/*
+	 * The WDMA RX driver sets RX_DRV_INIT_WDMA_EN once, when the RX DMA
+	 * is enabled: the handshake of a working init, not a fault.  It is in
+	 * the error mask the vendor and mainline share, and this WED enables
+	 * the WDMA RX DMA (the v1 in mainline does not), so say it once at
+	 * debug level and keep the error line for the real bits.
+	 */
+	if (val & ~WED_EXT_INT_STATUS_RX_DRV_INIT_WDMA_EN) {
+		if (net_ratelimit())
+			pr_err("airoha_wed%d: error status=%08x\n",
+			       dev->hw->index, val);
+	} else if (val) {
+		pr_debug("airoha_wed%d: wdma rx driver initialised\n",
+			 dev->hw->index);
+	}
 
 	val = wed_r32(dev, WED_INT_STATUS);
 	val &= mask;
